# Profile page — tile width is locked

On the **Profil** page (`profile_tab`), **never** change tile / card / page **width** unless the user explicitly asks for it.

## Forbidden without an explicit ask

- Page side margins / insets (`OuterMargin`, `PageMargin`, `PAGE_MARGIN`, scrollbar “compensation”)
- Forcing content width (`custom_minimum_size.x`, `_constrain_to_page_width`, swipe page width hacks)
- Stretch ratios, expand flags, or layout restructures whose goal is to make tiles narrower/wider
- Anything that makes profile content spill onto a neighbouring swipe tab in order to “fix” width

## Preferred conflict handling

If text / icons / separators fight for space:

- Prefer **overlap**, clipping, or smaller typography **only if the user asks**
- Do **not** widen/narrow tiles or page gutters to resolve the conflict
- Only move/resize **elements inside** a tile (text, icons, separators, vertical padding) when asked

## Allowed without a width ask

- Height of a tile (when the user asks)
- Internal layout: icon size, font size, vertical offsets, separators
- Colours, copy, data binding

If unsure whether a change affects tile width, **ask first** or skip it.
